Revision history for App-Clod

0.002 (not yet released)
    - Tell an answer to a review the base branch of its pull request.  A
      request to rebase that names no branch goes onto that branch, and a
      rewrite of the branch gets conflicts resolved on both sides and the
      tests run, because no pre-commit hook checks it.  The sort writes
      out what a short request, such as "rebase", means.
    - Sort what waits on the bot's own pull request before changing it.  A
      run that can only read answers each question in its thread, and only
      a request for a change goes on to a run that can commit.  A mention on
      that pull request is sorted as well.  A question in a line comment
      went to the run that changes code, and its prompt asked for a change
      or a reason not to make one.
    - A reply that finds a request for a change on the pull request of
      someone else starts a fix.  It started work on the review comments,
      which can push only to a pull request of the bot, and failed.
    - Find who wrote a review on a pull request from its latest review or
      line comment, when the notification names no latest comment, or
      names the pull request itself.  A review of an authorized user was
      ignored, as asked for by nobody known.
    - An assignment to a pull request becomes work on the review comments
      if the pull request is the bot's own, and a review if it is not.  It
      was a fix, which took the pull request for an issue and opened a
      second pull request with the same change.
    - Make no job for work on the review comments when no review comment
      or comment waits for an answer.  A triage ran first and then found
      nothing to do.
    - Fail a fix or an answer to a review that made no commit because
      claude refused some of its calls, and name each refused call in the
      error.  Such a run finished as no change before, with a reply that
      said the change was made.
    - With run_as, the account that claude runs as brings its own Claude
      token.  sudo logged the token of the worker, which went through
      --preserve-env, with its value.
    - Allow each Bash permission rule for the command that rtk makes of it,
      so that an unattended run is not refused every git and prove.
    - Make a new repository when an authorized user asks for one, if
      create_repos names the organizations where the bot may, then work in it
      like any other spoke and open an issue for its first release.
    - File a follow-up issue in a spoke when an authorized user asks for one,
      assigned to them, with follow_up_max as the cap of one request.

0.001 2026-10-28 TEODESIAN
    - Initial Release
